        "answer": {
          "short": "(II)",
          "worked": "The break point is $x=1$.\n\nFor $y=x-1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=1-1\\\\y&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThe endpoint $(1,0)$ is closed because $x\\ge 1$.\n\nFor $y=-x$, substituting $x=1$ gives $y=-1$. The endpoint $(1,-1)$ is open because $x<1$. The left branch descends through the origin and the right branch rises.\n\nGraph (II).",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
