        "answer": {
          "short": "(V)",
          "worked": "The break point is $x=1$.\n\nFor $y=x$, substituting $x=1$ gives $y=1$. The endpoint $(1,1)$ is closed because $x\\ge 1$.\n\nFor $y=x-1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=1-1\\\\y&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThe endpoint $(1,0)$ is open because $x<1$. Both branches have gradient $1$, so they are parallel and rise from left to right.\n\nGraph (V).",
